                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1afc790e-b880-3a40-9efe-81b3821d8c39",
                        "entry_id": "44f5aa4c-725a-376a-bb5a-e250175f565b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. странность, причуда, помешательство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e3addc0-4d56-46e7-93f5-9ebf3ba10abd",
                                "sense_id": "1afc790e-b880-3a40-9efe-81b3821d8c39",
                                "text": "— Ты видел, — проворчал Буратино, — у неё бзик в голове умыться, чистить зубы!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "516f91c0-c82e-4282-ae8f-7a15fc066efb",
                                "sense_id": "1afc790e-b880-3a40-9efe-81b3821d8c39",
                                "text": "— Пойми же, он сумасшедший, — повторял Франц. — Я знаю, что он сумасшедший… — Пустяки. Не сумасшедший, а просто так, с бзиком."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bbd7b6f3-af0b-4d6a-80ee-f257f51f5632",
                        "source_entry_id": "44f5aa4c-725a-376a-bb5a-e250175f565b",
                        "source_sense_id": "1afc790e-b880-3a40-9efe-81b3821d8c39",
                        "target_lang_word": "quirk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quirk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61a79917-94e8-3297-bebf-46b8bc99594c",
                                        "entry_id": "73e41c28-6af7-3aa1-b97b-3163f2751f45",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An idiosyncrasy; a slight glitch, a mannerism; something unusual about the manner or style of something or someone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "559ee594-c91e-4b84-97cc-769430eea5e7",
                                                "sense_id": "61a79917-94e8-3297-bebf-46b8bc99594c",
                                                "text": "The car steers cleanly, but the gearshift has a few quirks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53f5400c-a534-38b5-a471-e7a1a72c99cb",
                                        "entry_id": "73e41c28-6af7-3aa1-b97b-3163f2751f45",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An acute angle dividing a molding; a groove that runs lengthwise between the upper part of a molding and a soffit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67eac2f1-780c-37dc-a930-559c083e1ea2",
                                        "entry_id": "73e41c28-6af7-3aa1-b97b-3163f2751f45",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quibble, evasion, or subterfuge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a258fdb1-11ea-4789-b3db-f4e5e08bdfbb",
                                                "sense_id": "67eac2f1-780c-37dc-a930-559c083e1ea2",
                                                "text": "Had you no quirk / To avoid gullage, sir, by such a creature?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b5117ae-a113-43cb-9e46-60f8d4f41df4",
                                                "sense_id": "67eac2f1-780c-37dc-a930-559c083e1ea2",
                                                "text": "Let us not be too curious in prying into Gods arke, leaſt vve ſmart like the flie fluttering about the candle, for God is a conſuming fire to thoſe that vvill be ſporting themſelves in the quirks of their vvit about his ſacred myſteries."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quirk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50be1377-da11-31a2-892a-9a2bd695fab6",
                                        "entry_id": "3e207d83-d7ca-3807-b3a3-84191f5a1ed2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To (cause to) move with a wry jerk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1836fbf1-1ae1-4b4d-ac22-29fb7d57ef0b",
                                                "sense_id": "50be1377-da11-31a2-892a-9a2bd695fab6",
                                                "text": "He quirked an eyebrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b876765-f007-4530-9103-0dc61257a119",
                                                "sense_id": "50be1377-da11-31a2-892a-9a2bd695fab6",
                                                "text": "The corners of her mouth quirked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7af78b25-7d1f-400d-b489-0dd49de695d4",
                                                "sense_id": "50be1377-da11-31a2-892a-9a2bd695fab6",
                                                "text": "He quirked his lips playfully."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "546c3dd1-a8c6-37e1-97c2-4dd792f4e531",
                                        "entry_id": "3e207d83-d7ca-3807-b3a3-84191f5a1ed2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To furnish with a quirk or channel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a0541b5-0c81-35db-9ef0-0986981c80f4",
                                        "entry_id": "3e207d83-d7ca-3807-b3a3-84191f5a1ed2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To alter in a unique and unusual way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "684c78bf-2d78-403c-8ff4-7327e248a57c",
                                                "sense_id": "8a0541b5-0c81-35db-9ef0-0986981c80f4",
                                                "text": "But in the dream the forms are quirked by the peculiar troubles of the dreamer, whereas in myth the problems and solutions shown are directly valid for all mankind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e151b22d-2055-3d3a-8370-1c4c461b8261",
                                        "entry_id": "3e207d83-d7ca-3807-b3a3-84191f5a1ed2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use verbal tricks or quibbles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8be63588-a15e-4da5-80f3-7235b579a03b",
                                                "sense_id": "e151b22d-2055-3d3a-8370-1c4c461b8261",
                                                "text": "I have stung her and wrung her,\nThe venom is working;—\nAnd if you had hung her\nWith canting and quirking,\nShe could not be deader than she will be soon"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "quirk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bf012bf-93c0-3303-8f93-61906dedbe3f",
                                        "entry_id": "f1e2c203-cf5b-3d75-81f7-3e4cdc960cb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of querk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d6b6d44-75d6-4895-b2d6-24e8ab166003",
                        "source_entry_id": "44f5aa4c-725a-376a-bb5a-e250175f565b",
                        "source_sense_id": "1afc790e-b880-3a40-9efe-81b3821d8c39",
                        "target_lang_word": "whim",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whim",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                        "entry_id": "ff1fd901-60b4-32d7-95e0-a7807734cfd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fanciful impulse, or sudden change of idea."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e896ede-beb5-441f-9a84-fe9f250d66ac",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "Let ev’ry Man enjoy his whim; / What’s He to Me, or I to him?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b51de581-69ed-47ee-890d-e8d3a3283099",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "The king was tired of this whim of hers long ago, and thought she ought to get married like other people; there was nothing she need wait for, she was old enough and she would not be any richer either, for she was to have half the kingdom, which she inherited after her mother."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f38383f-7e86-48d8-ab88-bf281d714d64",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "“You’re either with me or you’re against me” became Dany’s credo, and those against her were an ever-changing multitude to be determined solely by her whims."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d78c190-eaea-4acf-ac9b-d6b4661d2691",
                                                "sense_id": "278fa71e-d392-3bb6-b0ed-1b262626f305",
                                                "text": "He also disagreed with the idea of cancelling projects \"completely at the whim of an individual Prime Minister,\" citing Rishi Sunak's decision to cancel HS2 north of Handsacre Junction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c84913e7-275a-399d-826b-59c394c8ead4",
                                        "entry_id": "ff1fd901-60b4-32d7-95e0-a7807734cfd3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large capstan or vertical drum turned by horse power or steam power, for raising ore or water, etc., from mines, or for other purposes"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
